210
00:33:30,014 --> 00:33:34,714
嫌われ方や 慕われ方や 叱り方とか 綺麗なぶつかり方
How to be disliked, how to be admired, how to scold, how to clash gracefully.

211
00:33:35,214 --> 00:33:38,714
もっと覚えたい事が山のようにある
There's still a mountain of things left to learn.

212
00:33:39,414 --> 00:33:41,714
のびしろしか無いわ
I've got nothing but room to grow!

213
00:33:42,014 --> 00:33:44,214
のびしろしか無いわ
Nothing but room to grow!

214
00:33:44,414 --> 00:33:46,714
のびしろしか無いわ
Nothing but room to grow!

215
00:33:47,014 --> 00:33:49,414
のびしろしか無いわ
Nothing but room to grow!

216
00:33:49,714 --> 00:33:52,014
俺らまだのびしろしかないわ
We still have nothing but room to grow!

217
00:33:52,214 --> 00:33:57,214
悪者扱いして来た街で 悪者扱いして来たオトナへ
To the streets I treated like villains, to the adults I treated like villains...

218
00:33:57,414 --> 00:34:02,214
変わりゆく俺 鏡の中へ 尋ねても答えならyeah yeah yeah
To the changing me inside the mirror, asking for an answer, yeah yeah yeah...

219
00:34:03,214 --> 00:34:06,214
去る者追わない引くとこ引いて 丸く収めたり
I won't chase those who leave, drawing back where I should, smoothing things over...

220
00:34:06,414 --> 00:34:10,714
軽くいなして 鏡の中でわろてるお前
Brushing it aside easily, smiling back at you inside the mirror.

221
00:34:11,214 --> 00:34:14,214
括れやしなかったわ たったの三文字で
Couldn't sum it up with just three words.

222
00:34:14,714 --> 00:34:19,714
日々重くなる足取りで 自分の歩幅で闊歩してる
Walking with steps growing heavier by the day, striding at my own pace.

223
00:34:20,014 --> 00:34:24,714
カマすとこカマス まかすとこまかす 割と適当な段取りで
Hitting hard where it counts, leaving it to chance where needed, with a somewhat casual setup.

224
00:34:25,014 --> 00:34:29,714
やっと分かって来たかも このポンコツの操縦の仕方を
I might finally be figuring out how to pilot this piece-of-junk self.

225
00:34:30,014 --> 00:34:35,414
19の時の「ついに来たか...」より もっと清々しい気持ち 隅田川にかかる
Feeling even fresher than the 'It's finally here...' when I was 19, crossing the Sumida River.

226
00:34:35,714 --> 00:34:40,714
勝鬨橋を渡る 左手にスカイツリー
Crossing Kachidoki Bridge, Skytree on the left...

227
00:34:41,214 --> 00:34:46,414
左手にスカイツリー 右手に東京タワー 俺はその真ん中
Skytree on the left, Tokyo Tower on the right, I'm right in the middle.

228
